      "Anticleia, and the arms that close on nothing": "Drinks, recognises her son, and gives him the state of his house: Penelope still there and still weeping, Telemachus running the estates, Laertes sleeping in the ashes in winter. She says she died of no sickness — it was longing for him and for his kindness that took her life. Then she goes through his arms three times and explains what the dead are.",
