      "Antinous and the web of Laertes": "Is accused in open assembly of a three-year fraud: a great shroud for Laertes woven by day and unpicked by torchlight, undone at last by a maid who told the suitors. Antinous presents it as proof of bad faith; the poem presents it as the only weapon available.",
